  --title "fix(ui): eliminate theme flash on load" \
  --body "## Problem
The dark/light mode was causing a severe flash (\"epilepsy effect\") on every page load.

**Root cause:** The \`ThemeProvider\` was applying the \`.dark\` / \`.light\` class inside a React \`useEffect\`, which runs *after* the browser has already painted the page. This caused a visible flash: the page first renders in the wrong theme (light) then jumps to the correct one (dark).

## Fix

1. **\`layout.tsx\`** — Added a tiny inline \`<script>\` in \`<head>\` that runs *synchronously before React renders*. It reads the saved theme from \`localStorage\` and applies the class to \`<html>\` immediately — zero flash.

\`\`\`js
(function(){
  try {
    var t = localStorage.getItem('agent-studio:theme');
    var r = t==='dark' ? 'dark' : t==='light' ? 'light'
          : window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
    document.documentElement.classList.add(r);
  } catch(e) {}
})();
\`\`\`

2. **\`ThemeContext.tsx\`** — The \`useEffect\` no longer touches the DOM (the script already did it). It only syncs React state to match the class that's already on \`<html>\`.

## Validation
- \`npx tsc --noEmit\` ✅
- \`npx next build\` ✅ (clean, no errors)" \
  --base main \
  --head fix/no-theme-flash

